  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml states no <repository>.",
        "  <repository> is the only machine-readable link from a published release back to the source it was built from, and <bugs> is where the App Store page sends a report. Without them a user of the release has no way back to the project."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json), AGPL (composer.json), LICENSES/ holds AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt, Apache-2.0.txt, BSD-2-Clause.txt, BSD-3-Clause.txt, CC0-1.0.txt, GPL-3.0-or-later.txt, ISC.txt, MIT.txt, MPL-2.0.txt.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 32 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  No SPDX id: AGPL (composer.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^22.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it.",
        "  The workflows read node-version from a variable, which is not resolved here, so whether CI builds on that major is not decidable from the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.js, superseded form), Stylelint (stylelint.config.js), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.integration.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), REUSE (REUSE.toml).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.js: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "1 declared package is named nowhere in the checkout: babel-loader-exclude-node-modules-except.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 220 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "versions-agree",
      "lines": [
        "Version 4.0.0 in appinfo/info.xml and package.json."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 32 to 32; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3) and composer.lock in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines).",
        "  make reads GNUmakefile and never Makefile; it runs only with make -f <name>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "Every directory the shipped PHP reaches through __DIR__ and the frontend through linkTo is in the shipped file set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk)."
      ]
    }
